\begin_layout Subsection
Analytical references: exact Euler-Bernoulli and Rayleigh-Ritz
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Two semi-analytical methods are kept beside the finite elements. The exact Euler-Bernoulli solution of a piecewise-uniform beam is obtained with transfer matrices 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
after ""
before ""
key "pestel1963"
literal "true"

\end_inset
: each tapered section is cut into 40 uniform steps, the four-by-four transfer matrices are multiplied from the clamp to the free end, and the natural frequencies are the roots of the resulting determinant. The Rayleigh-Ritz method projects the tongue on the first 
\begin_inset Formula $N$
\end_inset
 modes of a uniform cantilever; its integrals are computed exactly, section by section, by Gauss quadrature. The tool written in 2020 (km.py) and the time-domain model use 
\begin_inset Formula $N=2$
\end_inset
.
\end_layout

